-- The pharmacy and the clinic (tenth round): Fairview Pharmacy, the counter at the back of Fairview Market (Omar, the
-- pharmacist), and the walk-in clinic next to it (Grace, a nurse practitioner; no appointment needed). The voicemail of
-- day 10 (m10_pharmacy) now means something: the prescription is held for seven days, and picking it up takes a photo ID,
-- your date of birth and the copay. In free play you get sick now and then (a cold, or the flu, more in winter and after
-- a day soaked in the rain): symptoms and less energy in the morning, cold medicine from the pharmacy (not covered,
-- taxed), a visit to the clinic (the copay, a doctor's note for work, an antiviral for the flu in its first two days),
-- and a text to your manager to stay home. Out sick three working days in a row, HR asks for a doctor's note.
-- The conversations are tagged errand (not missions; the engine opens them when they apply) and one of pickup, otc, rx,
-- clinic (with cold or flu). What insurance leaves to you is config copay_* (the benefits plan may set it later).
-- No new tables or columns.














